WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:24.890 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.349 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:28.354 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of that day.

00:00:28.855 --> 00:00:30.911 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:32.673 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:33.873 --> 00:00:35.773 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:39.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:41.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A range is the top and the bottom,

00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:44.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two lines,

00:00:44.314 --> 00:00:46.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:47.132 --> 00:00:49.170 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.063 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the range.

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:53.482 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:53.482 --> 00:00:55.382 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.814 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in

00:00:57.814 --> 00:00:59.753 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:03.244 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:04.251 --> 00:01:06.096 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:06.096 --> 00:01:07.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:08.936 --> 00:01:11.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.524 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, range, levels and stop,

00:01:13.524 --> 00:01:15.775 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the pair, paper or a demo account,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.852 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
no secrets, a written stop, and

00:01:17.852 --> 00:01:20.189 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the word Example on every figure.

00:01:20.709 --> 00:01:22.090 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:23.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:23.951 --> 00:01:25.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:25.321 --> 00:01:27.109 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you drawing

00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:28.282 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a grid with no edges.

00:01:28.651 --> 00:01:30.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you buy

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.389 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and what you pay with.

00:01:31.763 --> 00:01:33.227 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:33.227 --> 00:01:34.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:35.281 --> 00:01:37.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:37.953 --> 00:01:39.684 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:39.977 --> 00:01:41.765 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:43.544 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair

00:01:43.544 --> 00:01:45.332 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:48.035 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:48.555 --> 00:01:49.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:01:49.974 --> 00:01:50.924 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of the day.

00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:52.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:54.433 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:55.245 --> 00:01:56.977 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:57.382 --> 00:01:59.967 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:04.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:07.347 --> 00:02:09.414 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

00:02:09.414 --> 00:02:11.593 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:12.026 --> 00:02:14.081 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:16.282 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if a daily close finishes outside

00:02:16.282 --> 00:02:18.337 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range and the next daily close

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:19.364 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is still outside.

00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:21.705 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:21.705 --> 00:02:23.373 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:23.893 --> 00:02:25.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:27.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:28.674 --> 00:02:30.797 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:31.113 --> 00:02:33.013 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:33.013 --> 00:02:34.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.337 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:36.337 --> 00:02:37.803 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:38.323 --> 00:02:41.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:43.749 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account,

00:02:43.749 --> 00:02:46.281 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and sometimes move money out of it.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.613 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:49.613 --> 00:02:52.153 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:54.472 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:54.992 --> 00:02:56.947 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:57.422 --> 00:02:59.053 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:00.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:01.889 --> 00:03:03.863 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the range onto the page,

00:03:03.863 --> 00:03:05.305 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not every day's prices.

00:03:05.825 --> 00:03:08.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:08.059 --> 00:03:10.207 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:10.727 --> 00:03:12.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the range.

00:03:13.944 --> 00:03:15.346 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.013 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, range,

00:03:18.013 --> 00:03:19.467 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:19.987 --> 00:03:22.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with no

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.269 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:24.789 --> 00:03:26.572 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.744 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the range

00:03:28.744 --> 00:03:30.838 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:30.838 --> 00:03:32.622 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:35.683 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:36.179 --> 00:03:38.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.101 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:40.621 --> 00:03:42.129 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.083 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:45.377 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:45.897 --> 00:03:47.294 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:47.809 --> 00:03:49.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.797 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:53.147 --> 00:03:54.990 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:55.374 --> 00:03:56.853 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:56.853 --> 00:03:58.261 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:03:58.781 --> 00:04:00.904 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:02.029 --> 00:04:03.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:03.606 --> 00:04:05.002 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:05.503 --> 00:04:07.235 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:10.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the July

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:13.852 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window, the public

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:16.544 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

00:04:16.544 --> 00:04:19.137 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October 2023, so you buy the base,

00:04:19.137 --> 00:04:21.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.622 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:25.142 --> 00:04:27.154 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:27.376 --> 00:04:28.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We price in US dollars.

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:31.229 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your exchange may charge fees

00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:32.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars, so

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.265 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
keep each in its own column.

00:04:34.763 --> 00:04:36.939 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:36.939 --> 00:04:39.115 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:39.115 --> 00:04:41.196 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:41.716 --> 00:04:43.622 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and

00:04:43.622 --> 00:04:46.138 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:47.188 --> 00:04:49.773 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:50.529 --> 00:04:55.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the July to October example window

00:04:55.508 --> 00:04:58.694 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:04:59.214 --> 00:05:00.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:05:01.114 --> 00:05:03.014 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:05:03.304 --> 00:05:05.463 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:05:05.463 --> 00:05:07.461 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:05:07.981 --> 00:05:09.837 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:05:09.837 --> 00:05:11.848 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:05:12.281 --> 00:05:14.407 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you got

00:05:14.407 --> 00:05:16.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.030 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.350 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.691 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to say what you will do.

00:05:22.141 --> 00:05:23.948 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places

00:05:23.948 --> 00:05:26.358 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:26.878 --> 00:05:29.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the range,

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom,

00:05:30.757 --> 00:05:32.879 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the second close still outside.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.963 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:34.963 --> 00:05:36.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders,

00:05:36.551 --> 00:05:38.451 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:38.963 --> 00:05:40.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:41.712 --> 00:05:44.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.476 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:49.476 --> 00:05:51.276 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:51.796 --> 00:05:54.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:05:54.098 --> 00:05:56.030 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:58.258 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the exchange runs it, not this course.

00:05:58.778 --> 00:06:00.782 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:06:00.782 --> 00:06:02.637 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:06:03.157 --> 00:06:05.224 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:06:05.224 --> 00:06:06.789 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:06:07.049 --> 00:06:09.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services

00:06:09.591 --> 00:06:12.210 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.830 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:17.661 --> 00:06:18.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:18.926 --> 00:06:20.266 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:20.777 --> 00:06:22.956 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:23.429 --> 00:06:25.719 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:26.146 --> 00:06:28.381 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.255 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:31.775 --> 00:06:33.706 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:33.706 --> 00:06:34.968 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:35.488 --> 00:06:38.429 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, platforms that hold

00:06:38.429 --> 00:06:41.272 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto for you need an ASIC licence,

00:06:41.272 --> 00:06:44.213 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a transition period to October

00:06:44.213 --> 00:06:47.350 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2027 for platforms already operating.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.881 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:50.128 --> 00:06:52.109 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:52.109 --> 00:06:53.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:06:54.593 --> 00:06:56.831 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your password,

00:06:56.831 --> 00:06:58.708 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is two-factor authentication.

00:06:59.228 --> 00:07:01.328 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:07:01.848 --> 00:07:03.881 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:05.989 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:08.129 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:07:09.179 --> 00:07:10.687 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is when your waiting

00:07:10.687 --> 00:07:11.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order actually trades.

00:07:12.494 --> 00:07:14.785 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:07:14.785 --> 00:07:16.908 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:17.118 --> 00:07:18.794 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:18.794 --> 00:07:20.526 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:20.862 --> 00:07:22.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.259 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:24.779 --> 00:07:26.231 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:26.231 --> 00:07:27.684 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:28.093 --> 00:07:30.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:31.435 --> 00:07:34.515 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:34.515 --> 00:07:37.276 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:37.796 --> 00:07:39.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:42.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:42.084 --> 00:07:44.016 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:44.536 --> 00:07:46.574 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:47.094 --> 00:07:48.156 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the July

00:07:48.156 --> 00:07:49.826 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window.

00:07:50.346 --> 00:07:52.658 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:52.658 --> 00:07:55.134 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:07:55.134 --> 00:07:57.776 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:07:58.296 --> 00:08:00.250 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
To compare them, turn the gap into

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.422 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a percent by dividing it by the price.

00:08:02.942 --> 00:08:05.939 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the lesson 1 example, 900

00:08:05.939 --> 00:08:09.345 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by 27,630 is about 3.3

00:08:09.345 --> 00:08:12.887 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, well above 0.2 percent.

00:08:13.407 --> 00:08:14.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:08:14.951 --> 00:08:16.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:18.862 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:08:19.495 --> 00:08:21.381 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin built

00:08:21.381 --> 00:08:23.595 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay worth about one US dollar.

00:08:24.115 --> 00:08:25.735 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:08:26.204 --> 00:08:28.657 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If your pair is priced in a stablecoin,

00:08:28.657 --> 00:08:31.190 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill trades one coin for another,

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.614 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every fill is a swap.

00:08:33.664 --> 00:08:35.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated record

00:08:35.869 --> 00:08:37.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of every bot: the plan,

00:08:37.162 --> 00:08:39.063 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the changes, the fills, the fees,

00:08:39.063 --> 00:08:40.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a review note of what happened,

00:08:40.964 --> 00:08:43.170 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and whether you followed the rules.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.477 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:45.826 --> 00:08:47.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.793 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

00:08:50.793 --> 00:08:52.743 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every swap goes in the journal.

00:08:53.263 --> 00:08:55.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is also the page you will

00:08:55.548 --> 00:08:57.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:08:58.277 --> 00:09:00.802 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:09:00.802 --> 00:09:02.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

00:09:02.854 --> 00:09:05.301 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the value

00:09:05.301 --> 00:09:07.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars at the time,

00:09:07.511 --> 00:09:09.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

00:09:09.957 --> 00:09:12.246 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it was for, and who the other side was.

00:09:12.766 --> 00:09:14.840 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.607 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, the gaps, the money

00:09:16.607 --> 00:09:18.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in the bot, the stop rule,

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.217 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fills, the fees, the Australian

00:09:20.217 --> 00:09:22.368 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar value of each fill, a review

00:09:22.368 --> 00:09:24.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:09:24.886 --> 00:09:26.523 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The Australian dollar value

00:09:26.523 --> 00:09:28.092 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column is the one exception.

00:09:28.612 --> 00:09:30.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is for your tax records.

00:09:30.637 --> 00:09:32.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.752 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:09:35.173 --> 00:09:36.178 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records

00:09:36.178 --> 00:09:37.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for at least five years.

00:09:37.875 --> 00:09:39.647 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:09:39.647 --> 00:09:40.534 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:09:41.054 --> 00:09:42.841 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.424 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:44.944 --> 00:09:47.234 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:47.368 --> 00:09:48.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:48.991 --> 00:09:50.834 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:51.495 --> 00:09:53.885 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask

00:09:53.885 --> 00:09:55.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for a seed phrase, a private

00:09:55.833 --> 00:09:57.250 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:59.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:09:59.746 --> 00:10:01.168 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, or asks for one

00:10:01.168 --> 00:10:02.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of those, treat it as a scam.

00:10:03.348 --> 00:10:04.577 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:10:05.589 --> 00:10:08.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:10:08.084 --> 00:10:10.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:10:10.806 --> 00:10:11.811 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:10:12.802 --> 00:10:15.105 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now cover the chart and say your page

00:10:15.105 --> 00:10:16.795 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
out loud: the pair, the range,

00:10:16.795 --> 00:10:18.407 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the stop rule.

00:10:18.927 --> 00:10:20.928 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

00:10:20.928 --> 00:10:22.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:10:23.141 --> 00:10:25.261 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:10:25.261 --> 00:10:27.381 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:10:27.901 --> 00:10:30.006 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase,

00:10:30.006 --> 00:10:32.533 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a private key, or an API secret.

00:10:33.053 --> 00:10:34.729 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:10:35.127 --> 00:10:37.365 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own notebook

00:10:37.365 --> 00:10:39.392 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so a practice sketch is never later

00:10:39.392 --> 00:10:40.791 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
mistaken for a live plan.

00:10:41.841 --> 00:10:44.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.362 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:46.362 --> 00:10:48.662 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:49.862 --> 00:10:51.276 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: How a grid

00:10:51.276 --> 00:10:52.847 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot works, order by order.

00:10:53.367 --> 00:10:54.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your range,

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:56.608 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:10:56.849 --> 00:10:58.071 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example

00:10:58.071 --> 00:10:59.497 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on every practice figure.

00:11:00.017 --> 00:11:01.665 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:11:01.665 --> 00:11:03.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

